{"chunk_id": "e059f9f88b52", "text": "As Shatrughna battles the demon Lavana, the gods gather in the sky to witness the climactic moment. Shatrughna unleashes a radiant celestial weapon whose brilliance resembles the fire that ends the universe. His arrow pierces Lavana\u2019s chest, descends even into the netherworld, and then returns to its master; the demon collapses like a mountain struck by lightning. With the terror of the three worlds destroyed, the gods rejoice and offer Shatrughna a boon. He asks to rule the beautiful city built by the gods, and they grant it, naming it Shurashena. Shatrughna summons his army and establishes prosperous rule there. For twelve peaceful years the land flourishes under his protection, until he finally longs to see his brother Rama again, prompting a future return to Ayodhya.\nShatrughna slays the demon Lavana, receives a boon from the gods, rules Madhu\u2019s city as Shurasena in prosperity, and later longs to see Rama again.\nThemes: demon slaying, divine blessing, kingship and governance, prosperous city, devotion to Rama", "vector": [0.01655086874961853, -0.010431332513689995, -0.0028840156737715006, -0.0053596156649291515, -0.0048507703468203545, 0.016751728951931, -0.028227534145116806, -0.017541779205203056, -0.02980763278901577, -0.025214632973074913, 0.015077894553542137, 0.017354309558868408, 0.005851722788065672, 0.020474335178732872, 0.003342646174132824, 0.011141037568449974, 0.042100269347429276, -0.024384411051869392, 0.022536497563123703, -0.013517881743609905, -0.001799371326342225, -0.006179794669151306, -0.008195090107619762, 0.023152468726038933, -0.02919166162610054, 0.007793370168656111, 0.013939687982201576, -0.03543171286582947, 0.009527461603283882, -0.00043561524944379926, -0.006544690113514662, -0.008395950309932232, -0.007244352716952562, -0.004763730801641941, -0.03979707136750221, 0.010973654687404633, -0.0009658021153882146, -0.007184094749391079, 0.010598715394735336, 0.011710141785442829, -0.0018